          <span id="shareBtnLabel">Share Link</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Full weight table -->
    <section class="mt-10" aria-label="Reducer weight table">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">ASME B16.9 Reducer Weights — <span id="tableTitle" class="accent-text">Concentric SCH 40 Reference</span></h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl bg-theme-card shadow-md">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[720px] text-sm">
          <thead class="bg-ink-900 text-left text-xs uppercase tracking-wider text-theme-secondary">
            <tr>
              <th class="px-3 py-2.5">Combination</th>
              <th class="px-3 py-2.5">Large OD (mm)</th>
              <th class="px-3 py-2.5">Small OD (mm)</th>
              <th class="px-3 py-2.5">H ≈ (mm)</th>
              <th class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right">SCH 40 CON</th>
              <th class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right">SCH 80 CON</th>
              <th class="px-3 py-2.5 text-right">SCH 40 ECC</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody id="weightTableBody" class="divide-y divide-theme"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-theme-muted">Table weights use the currently selected material density and are shown in <span id="tableUnit">kg</span>. Tap any row to load it into the calculator.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Methodology -->
    <section class="mt-12" aria-label="Calculation methodology">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">How the calculation works <span class="accent-text">(large-end pipe weight × calibration factors)</span></h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="card">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 420 240" class="w-full" role="img" aria-label="Concentric and eccentric reducer geometric model">
            <defs>
              <marker id="arrR" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="6" markerHeight="6" orient="auto-start-reverse">
                <path d="M0 0 L10 5 L0 10 z" fill="#64748b" />
              </marker>
            </defs>
            <!-- concentric reducer -->
            <path d="M60 60 L300 86 L300 154 L60 180 Z" fill="#fed7aa" opacity="0.5" stroke="#c2410c" stroke-width="2" />
            <line x1="60" y1="60" x2="60" y2="180" stroke="#c2410c" stroke-width="2" />
            <line x1="300" y1="86" x2="300" y2="154" stroke="#c2410c" stroke-width="2" />
            <line x1="20" y1="120" x2="330" y2="120" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="6 5" />
            <text x="180" y="42" font-size="12" fill="#9a3412" text-anchor="middle">Concentric — center lines aligned</text>
            <!-- D dim -->
            <line x1="44" y1="60" x2="44" y2="180" stroke="#64748b" marker-start="url(#arrR)" marker-end="url(#arrR)" />
            <text x="30" y="124" font-size="11" fill="#334155">D</text>
            <!-- d dim -->
            <line x1="316" y1="86" x2="316" y2="154" stroke="#64748b" marker-start="url(#arrR)" marker-end="url(#arrR)" />
            <text x="332" y="124" font-size="11" fill="#334155">d</text>
            <!-- H dim -->
            <line x1="60" y1="202" x2="300" y2="202" stroke="#64748b" marker-start="url(#arrR)" marker-end="url(#arrR)" />
            <text x="180" y="218" font-size="11" fill="#334155" text-anchor="middle">H ≈ large-end OD (typ. manufacturer length)</text>
            <!-- eccentric reducer -->
            <path d="M60 226 L300 226 L300 214 L60 190 Z" fill="#fde68a" opacity="0.6" stroke="#b45309" stroke-width="2" />
            <text x="180" y="182" font-size="11" fill="#92400e" text-anchor="middle">Eccentric — flat bottom (≈ +6% weight)</text>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="card text-sm leading-relaxed text-theme-secondary">
          <p class="font-semibold text-theme-primary">Reducer weight equations (ASME B16.9 + ASME B36.10M)</p>
          <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5">
            <li><strong>Base method:</strong> W<sub>con</sub> ≈ 0.80 × straight-pipe weight of the <strong>large end</strong> size &amp; schedule · W<sub>ecc</sub> ≈ 0.85 ×</li>
            <li><strong>This calculator (catalog-calibrated):</strong> W = W<sub>ref</sub>(large × small, SCH 40) × F<sub>sch</sub> × F<sub>type</sub> × (ρ / 7,850)</li>
            <li><strong>Schedule factor F<sub>sch</sub>:</strong> SCH 40 / STD = 1.0 · SCH 80 / XS = 1.5 · SCH 10–160 and XXS scale the SCH 40 reference by their ASME B36.10M metal-mass ratio</li>
            <li><strong>Type factor F<sub>type</sub>:</strong> concentric = 1.0 · eccentric = 1.06 (≈ 0.85 / 0.80)</li>
            <li><strong>Unlisted combinations:</strong> extrapolate from the nearest known combination, metal volume ∝ large-end NPS²</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="mt-3">The raw 0.8 × straight-pipe shortcut needs an assumed reducer length, which ASME B16.9 does not standardize — manufacturer end-to-end lengths vary by roughly ±30%. Anchoring on catalog weights for the actual large × small combination removes that guesswork: for a 6″ × 4″ SCH 40 reducer the engine returns ≈ 2.5 kg, matching supplier catalogs, where a naive 0.8 × kg/m × OD estimate can drift ±25%.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SEO content -->
    <section class="mt-12 space-y-6" aria-label="Reducer weight reference guide">
      <div class="card">
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">How to Calculate Reducer Weight</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-theme-secondary">
          <p>To calculate the weight of a butt-weld reducer you need five inputs: the reducer type (concentric or eccentric), the large-end NPS, the small-end NPS, the wall schedule and the material density. The small end must always be smaller than the large end — a reducer transitions between two different pipe sizes in the same line. Start from a catalog or calibrated concentric SCH 40 reference weight for the exact large × small combination, then multiply by the schedule factor (SCH 80 ≈ 1.5 × SCH 40), by 1.06 if the reducer is eccentric, and by the ratio of your material density to 7,850 kg/m³ if you are not working in carbon steel.</p>
          <p>Procurement and freight teams usually skip the geometry entirely and order by catalog weight, because reducer end-to-end lengths are manufacturer-specific. This calculator combines both worlds: calibrated reference weights for the 20 most common combinations, deterministic extrapolation ∝ large-end NPS² for the rest, and automatic schedule, type and material scaling — so a 10-piece bill of materials totals instantly in kg or lb.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">Reducer Weight Formula</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-theme-secondary">
          <p>The complete formula used by this calculator is:</p>
          <p class="rounded-lg bg-theme-tertiary px-4 py-3 font-mono text-sm text-theme-secondary">W = W_ref(large × small) × F_sch × F_type × ρ / 7,850</p>
          <p>where W_ref is the carbon-steel concentric SCH 40 reference weight for the selected combination, F_sch is the schedule factor (1.0 for SCH 40 / STD, 1.5 for SCH 80 / XS, metal-mass ratios for other schedules), F_type is 1.0 for concentric and 1.06 for eccentric, and ρ is the material density in kg/m³. Total weight for a purchase order is W × quantity. Worked example: a 6″ × 4″ SCH 80 eccentric reducer in stainless F316 (ρ = 7,980) weighs 2.50 × 1.5 × 1.06 × 7,980 / 7,850 ≈ 4.04 kg, and twenty pieces weigh ≈ 80.8 kg.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="card">
        <h2 class="mb-3 text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">ASME B16.9 Standard</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-theme-secondary">
          <p>ASME B16.9, “Factory-Made Wrought Buttwelding Fittings,” is the governing standard for butt-weld reducers in sizes NPS 1/2″ through 48″. It defines concentric reducers (center lines aligned) and eccentric reducers (offset bore, flat on one side) with beveled ends for butt welding. Unlike elbows and tees, B16.9 does not assign reducer end-to-end lengths — those follow manufacturer or purchaser agreement (MSS SP-43 / SP-75 for stainless and other fittings), which is why reducer weights are best anchored on catalog values rather than envelope geometry.</p>
          <p>Wall thicknesses follow ASME B36.10M for carbon and alloy steel (SCH 10, 20, 30, STD, 40, 60, XS, 80, 100, 120, 140, 160, XXS) and ASME B36.19M for stainless steel. Typical materials include ASTM A234 WPB (carbon steel), A403 WP304/WP316 (stainless) and A234 WP11/WP22 (alloy steel). Eccentric reducers are standard in horizontal pump suction lines where a flat bottom prevents air pockets, while concentric reducers suit vertical runs and general process piping.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="mt-12" aria-label="Frequently asked questions">
      <h2 class="mb-4 text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <div class="space-y-3">
        {faqs.map((f) => (
          <details class="group card open:shadow-md">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer list-none px-5 py-3.5 text-sm font-semibold text-theme-secondary marker:hidden group-open:accent-text">
              {f.q}
              <span class="float-right text-theme-muted transition group-open:rotate-45 group-open:accent-text">+</span>
            </summary>
            <p class="px-5 pb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-theme-secondary">{f.a}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Internal links -->
    <section class="mt-12 rounded-xl bg-ink-900 border border-theme p-6 text-theme-primary" aria-label="Related tools">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-lg font-bold">Related Engineering Tools</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 text-sm sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
        <a href="/flange-weight-calculator/" class="rounded-lg bg-ink-800 p-3 transition hover:bg-ink-700">→ Flange Weight Calculator</a>
        <a href="/elbow-weight-calculator/" class="rounded-lg bg-ink-800 p-3 transition hover:bg-ink-700">→ Elbow Weight Calculator</a>
        <a href="/tee-weight-calculator/" class="rounded-lg bg-ink-800 p-3 transition hover:bg-ink-700">→ Tee Weight Calculator</a>
        <a href="/products/concentric-reducer/" class="rounded-lg bg-ink-800 p-3 transition hover:bg-ink-700">→ Reducer Product Specs</a>
        <a href="/request-a-quote/" class="rounded-lg accent-bg p-3 font-semibold transition hover:opacity-90 text-ink-950">→ Request a Quote</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Disclaimer -->
    <p class="mt-8 disclaimer rounded-lg p-4 text-xs leading-relaxed">
      <strong>Disclaimer:</strong> Calculated weights are theoretical values based on ASME B16.9
      reducer combinations and catalog-calibrated reference weights for carbon steel.
      Actual fitting weights vary between manufacturers because B16.9 does not standardize
      reducer end-to-end lengths and permits tolerances on wall thickness. For critical
      applications (lifting, shipping cost guarantees, pressure-boundary design), verify
      with the fitting manufacturer.
    </p>
  
  </div>
</Base>

<script>
  import { COMBO_LIST, MATERIALS, NPS_LIST, REDUCER_TYPES, SCHEDULES, SMALL_END_MAX, type ReducerType } from '../data/reducer-dimensions';
  import { computeReducerWeight } from '../lib/reducer-calculations';

  const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;
  const state = {
    type: 'CON' as ReducerType,
    large: 6,
    small: 4,
    schedule: 'SCH40',
    density: 7850,
    qty: 1,
    unit: (localStorage.getItem('pvf_unit_pref') === 'lb' ? 'lb' : 'kg') as 'kg' | 'lb',
  };

  const fmt = (v: number, d = 2) =>
    v.toLocaleString('en-US', { minimumFractionDigits: d, maximumFractionDigits: d });

  function populateLarge() {
    const sel = $('largeNps') as HTMLSelectElement;
    sel.innerHTML = '';
    for (const n of NPS_LIST) {
      if (n.nps < 0.75) continue; // large ends: NPS 3/4" and up
      const opt = document.createElement('option');
      opt.value = String(n.nps);
      opt.textContent = n.label;
      if (n.nps === state.large) opt.selected = true;
      sel.appendChild(opt);
    }
  }

  function populateSmall() {
    const sel = $('smallNps') as HTMLSelectElement;
    sel.innerHTML = '';
    const valid = NPS_LIST.filter((n) => n.nps < state.large && n.nps <= SMALL_END_MAX);
    for (const n of valid) {
      const opt = document.createElement('option');
      opt.value = String(n.nps);
      opt.textContent = n.label;
      if (n.nps === state.small) opt.selected = true;
      sel.appendChild(opt);
    }
    if (!valid.some((n) => n.nps === state.small)) {
      state.small = valid.length ? valid[valid.length - 1].nps : 0;
      sel.value = String(state.small);
    }
  }

  function populateMaterials() {
    const sel = $('material') as HTMLSelectElement;
    sel.innerHTML = '';
    for (const m of MATERIALS) {
      const opt = document.createElement('option');
      opt.value = m.id;
      opt.textContent = `${m.name} (${m.standard}) — ${m.density} kg/m³`;
      sel.appendChild(opt);
    }
  }

  function setTypeStyles() {
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLLabelElement>('.type-opt').forEach((l) => {
      const active = l.dataset.type === state.type;
      l.classList.toggle('accent-border', active);
      l.classList.toggle('accent-light-bg', active);
      l.classList.toggle('accent-text', active);
      l.classList.toggle('border-theme', !active);
      l.classList.toggle('text-theme-secondary', !active);
    });
    const t = REDUCER_TYPES.find((x) => x.id === state.type);
    $('typeDesc').textContent = t ? `${t.name} — ${t.desc}` : '';
  }

  function setUnitButtons() {
    const on = 'bg-ink-900 text-theme-primary';
    const off = 'bg-theme-card text-theme-secondary hover:bg-theme-tertiary';
    $('unitKg').className = 'unit-btn flex-1 px-3 py-2 text-sm font-semibold transition ' + (state.unit === 'kg' ? on : off);
    $('unitLb').className = 'unit-btn flex-1 px-3 py-2 text-sm font-semibold transition ' + (state.unit === 'lb' ? on : off);
  }

  const scheduleName = (id: string) => SCHEDULES.find((s) => s.id === id)?.name ?? id;
  const typeName = (id: ReducerType) => (id === 'ECC' ? 'Eccentric' : 'Concentric');

  function renderResult() {
    const r = computeReducerWeight(state.type, state.large, state.small, state.schedule, state.density);
    const invalid = !r.valid;
    $('smallNote').classList.toggle('hidden', !invalid);
    ($('smallNps') as HTMLSelectElement).classList.toggle('accent-border', invalid);
    if (invalid) {
      $('weightValue').textContent = '–';
      $('resultLine').textContent = 'Select a small end smaller than the large end.';
      $('totalWeight').textContent = '–';
      return;
    }
    const w = state.unit === 'kg' ? r.weightKg : r.weightLb;
    $('weightValue').textContent = fmt(w, w >= 100 ? 1 : 2);
    $('weightUnit').textContent = state.unit;
    $('resultLine').textContent =
      `${typeName(r.type)} Reducer ${r.largeLabel} × ${r.smallLabel} ${scheduleName(r.schedule)} · ${MATERIALS.find((m) => m.id === ($('material') as HTMLSelectElement).value)?.name ?? ''}`;
    const total = w * state.qty;
    $('outQty').textContent = String(state.qty);
    $('totalWeight').textContent = `${fmt(total, total >= 100 ? 1 : 2)} ${state.unit}`;
    $('outLength').textContent = `${fmt(r.lengthMm, 1)} mm`;
    $('outLargeOd').textContent = `${fmt(r.largeOdMm, 1)} mm`;

    const rows: [string, string][] = [
      ['Reducer type', `${typeName(r.type)} (ASME B16.9)`],
      ['Combination', `${r.largeLabel} × ${r.smallLabel}`],
      ['Schedule', scheduleName(r.schedule)],
      ['Large-end OD × wall', `${fmt(r.largeOdMm, 1)} mm`],
      ['Small-end OD', `${fmt(r.smallOdMm, 1)} mm`],
      ['End-to-end (H, typ.)', `${fmt(r.lengthMm, 1)} mm`],
      ['Size ratio d/D', fmt(r.smallOdMm / r.largeOdMm, 3)],
    ];
    $('dimsList').innerHTML = rows
      .map(([k, v]) => `<div class="flex justify-between border-b border-theme py-1.5"><dt class="text-theme-muted">${k}</dt><dd class="font-semibold text-theme-secondary text-right">${v}</dd></div>`)
      .join('');

    const basis: [string, string][] = [
      ['SCH 40 CON reference', `${fmt(r.referenceKg, 2)} kg (CS)`],
      ['Schedule factor', `× ${fmt(r.scheduleFactor, 2)}`],
      ['Reducer-type factor', `× ${fmt(r.typeFactor, 2)}`],
      ['Density factor', `× ${fmt(state.density / 7850, 3)} (${fmt(state.density, 0)} kg/m³)`],
    ];
    $('basisList').innerHTML = basis
      .map(([k, v]) => `<div class="flex justify-between border-b border-theme py-1.5"><dt class="text-theme-muted">${k}</dt><dd class="font-semibold text-theme-secondary text-right">${v}</dd></div>`)
      .join('') +
      `<div class="flex justify-between py-1.5"><dt class="text-theme-muted">Result</dt><dd class="font-bold accent-text">${fmt(r.weightKg, 2)} kg</dd></div>`;
  }

  function renderTable() {
    $('tableUnit').textContent = state.unit;
    const tbody = $('weightTableBody');
    tbody.innerHTML = '';
    for (const c of COMBO_LIST) {
      const r40 = computeReducerWeight('CON', c.large, c.small, 'SCH40', state.density);
      const r80 = computeReducerWeight('CON', c.large, c.small, 'SCH80', state.density);
      const recc = computeReducerWeight('ECC', c.large, c.small, 'SCH40', state.density);
      if (!r40.valid) continue;
      const conv = (x: { weightKg: number; weightLb: number }) => (state.unit === 'kg' ? x.weightKg : x.weightLb);
      const isCurrent = state.large === c.large && state.small === c.small;
      const tr = document.createElement('tr');
      tr.className = 'cursor-pointer hover-accent-light' + (isCurrent ? ' accent-light-bg' : '');
      tr.innerHTML =
        `<td class="px-3 py-2 font-semibold">${r40.largeLabel} × ${r40.smallLabel}</td>` +
        `<td class="px-3 py-2">${fmt(r40.largeOdMm, 1)}</td>` +
        `<td class="px-3 py-2">${fmt(r40.smallOdMm, 1)}</td>` +
        `<td class="px-3 py-2">${fmt(r40.lengthMm, 1)}</td>` +
        `<td class="px-3 py-2 text-right font-semibold ${isCurrent && state.type === 'CON' && (state.schedule === 'SCH40' || state.schedule === 'STD') ? 'accent-text' : ''}">${fmt(conv(r40), 2)}</td>` +
        `<td class="px-3 py-2 text-right font-semibold ${isCurrent && state.type === 'CON' && (state.schedule === 'SCH80' || state.schedule === 'XS') ? 'accent-text' : ''}">${fmt(conv(r80), 2)}</td>` +
        `<td class="px-3 py-2 text-right font-semibold ${isCurrent && state.type === 'ECC' && (state.schedule === 'SCH40' || state.schedule === 'STD') ? 'accent-text' : ''}">${fmt(conv(recc), 2)}</td>`;
      tr.addEventListener('click', () => {
        state.large = c.large;
        state.small = c.small;
        ($('largeNps') as HTMLSelectElement).value = String(c.large);
        populateSmall();
        ($('smallNps') as HTMLSelectElement).value = String(c.small);
        render();
        $('tool').scrollIntoView({ behavior: 'smooth', block: 'start' });
      });
      tbody.appendChild(tr);
    }
  }

  function render() {
    renderResult();
    renderTable();
  }

  // Events
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[name="rtype"]').forEach((radio) =>
    radio.addEventListener('change', () => {
      if (!radio.checked) return;
      state.type = radio.value as ReducerType;
      setTypeStyles();
      render();
    })
  );
  $('largeNps').addEventListener('change', (e) => {
    state.large = Number((e.target as HTMLSelectElement).value);
    populateSmall(); // small end options are always < large end
    render();
  });
  $('smallNps').addEventListener('change', (e) => { state.small = Number((e.target as HTMLSelectElement).value); render(); });
  $('schedule').addEventListener('change', (e) => { state.schedule = (e.target as HTMLSelectElement).value; render(); });
  $('material').addEventListener('change', (e) => {
    const m = MATERIALS.find((x) => x.id === (e.target as HTMLSelectElement).value)!;
    state.density = m.density;
    ($('density') as HTMLInputElement).value = String(m.density);
    ($('density') as HTMLInputElement).disabled = m.id !== 'custom';
    render();
  });
  $('density').addEventListener('input', (e) => {
    const v = Number((e.target as HTMLInputElement).value);
    if (v > 0) { state.density = v; render(); }
  });
  $('qty').addEventListener('input', (e) => {
    const v = Math.max(1, Math.floor(Number((e.target as HTMLSelectElement).value) || 1));
    state.qty = v;
    renderResult();
  });
  $('unitKg').addEventListener('click', () => { state.unit = 'kg'; localStorage.setItem('pvf_unit_pref', 'kg'); setUnitButtons(); render(); });
  $('unitLb').addEventListener('click', () => { state.unit = 'lb'; localStorage.setItem('pvf_unit_pref', 'lb'); setUnitButtons(); render(); });

  // Init
  populateMaterials();
  ($('density') as HTMLInputElement).disabled = true;
  populateLarge();
  populateSmall();
  setTypeStyles();
  setUnitButtons();
  render();

  // Copy Result
  $('copyBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
    const w = ($('weightValue') as HTMLElement).textContent ?? '–';
    const unit = ($('weightUnit') as HTMLElement).textContent ?? '';
    const line = ($('resultLine') as HTMLElement).textContent ?? '';
    const total = ($('totalWeight') as HTMLElement).textContent ?? '–';
    const qty = ($('outQty') as HTMLElement).textContent ?? '1';
    const text = `PVF Calculator — Reducer Weight\n${line}\nSingle: ${w} ${unit}  ·  Qty: ${qty}  ·  Total: ${total}\nhttps://pvfcalculator.com/reducer-weight-calculator/`;
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(() => {
      $('copyBtnLabel').textContent = '✓ Copied!';
      setTimeout(() => { $('copyBtnLabel').textContent = 'Copy Result'; }, 2000);
    });
  });

  // Share Link
  $('shareBtn').addEventListener('click', () => {
    const sp = new URLSearchParams({
      type: state.type, large: String(state.large), small: String(state.small),
      schedule: state.schedule, material: ($('material') as HTMLSelectElement).value,
      density: String(state.density), qty: String(state.qty), unit: state.unit,
    });
    history.replaceState(null, '', '?' + sp.toString());
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(location.href).then(() => {
      $('shareBtnLabel').textContent = '✓ Link copied!';
      setTimeout(() => { $('shareBtnLabel').textContent = 'Share Link'; }, 2000);
    });
  });

  // Restore from URL params on load
  {
    const sp = new URLSearchParams(location.search);
    let changed = false;
    const t = sp.get('type') as ReducerType;
    if (t && (['CON','ECC'] as string[]).includes(t)) { state.type = t; setTypeStyles(); document.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input[name="rtype"]').forEach((r) => { r.checked = r.value === t; }); changed = true; }
    const ln = Number(sp.get('large'));
    if (ln > 0) { state.large = ln; ($('largeNps') as HTMLSelectElement).value = String(ln); populateSmall(); changed = true; }
    const sn = Number(sp.get('small'));
    if (sn > 0) { state.small = sn; ($('smallNps') as HTMLSelectElement).value = String(sn); changed = true; }
    const sch = sp.get('schedule');
    if (sch) { state.schedule = sch; ($('schedule') as HTMLSelectElement).value = sch; changed = true; }
    const mat = sp.get('material');
    if (mat) { const found = MATERIALS.find((m) => m.id === mat); if (found) { ($('material') as HTMLSelectElement).value = mat; state.density = found.density; ($('density') as HTMLInputElement).value = String(found.density); ($('density') as HTMLInputElement).disabled = mat !== 'custom'; changed = true; } }
    const d = Number(sp.get('density'));
    if (d > 0) { state.density = d; ($('density') as HTMLInputElement).value = String(d); changed = true; }
    const q = Number(sp.get('qty'));
    if (q >= 1) { state.qty = Math.max(1, Math.floor(q)); ($('qty') as HTMLInputElement).value = String(state.qty); changed = true; }
    const u = sp.get('unit');
    if (u === 'kg' || u === 'lb') { state.unit = u; setUnitButtons(); changed = true; }
    if (changed) render();
  }
</script>
